WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.069
-Our first guest tonight is
a very talented actress you know

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.171
from her work
in "Baywatch" and "Quantico."

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.740
She stars in
"The Matrix Resurrections,"

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.209
which will be in theaters
and IMAX nationwide

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.111
and on HBO Max December 22nd.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:13.112
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.348
our friend
Priyanka Chopra Jonas.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.350
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:24.490 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:31.598 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.132
Hi. How are you?

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:36.035
-I'm just so happy to be back
with a live audience!

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.270
-Isn't it wonderful?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.606
-Oh, it's so special!

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.442
-I know, because I think
sometimes too much was put on

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:45.311
the fact that it was weird
for hosts to do it

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.180
without audiences, but guests
on talk shows, I feel like,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.348
needed audiences even more

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:50.450
because we got to do it
every day.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.851
We got more and more
used to the fact

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.353
that there was nobody here,
but it must have been so jarring

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.421
when you were doing press and
having to be in front of nobody.

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:58.057
-You're the first person --
like, the first late-night show

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.325
I'm doing in like two years.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.760
So I'm out of practice, guys.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.362
-No, no, you're off to it.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.697
Everybody already is thinking,
"She's really good at this."

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.132
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.167
-We'll find out.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.969
-You just passed
a three-year anniversary

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:10.904
to your husband, Nick Jonas?
-Yes.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.371
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:15.608
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.378
-I sort of felt like this was a
sign of a very strong marriage.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.547
I saw you burning him
with some zingers

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:23.049
at the Jonas brothers
family roast.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.751
Did you enjoy?
It must be fun to stand up --

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:27.654
I mean, 'cause, again,
he sort of signed up for it,

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.821
so you're allowed.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.056
-Oh, I had a great time.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.791
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.460
I mean, how often can you
actually really roast

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.661
your husband publicly,

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.531
and Netflix and the whole world
is watching?

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.667
It's like I have --
It was so much freedom.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.102
-When it was over,
did he give you --

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.770
Was he happy? Was he proud?

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.006
'Cause I would be proud,
no matter the burn,

00:01:48.006 --> 00:01:50.542
if they were as well-delivered
as you delivered them.

00:01:50.542 --> 00:01:52.144
-Okay, alright, I'll be honest.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:54.113
I'm going to give Nick credit
where it's due.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.949
He wrote half my jokes
because I was so nervous.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.017
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.151
-But you write half of
their songs?

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.686
-But I delivered them.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.555
Yes. I'm the muse.
-You're the muse.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.890
-So I basically write the songs.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.092
-There you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.693
That's very nice of you
to give him that credit.

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.163
Again, another sign of
a very strong marriage.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:13.098
-Secure, I guess.
-Exactly, secure marriage, yeah.

00:02:13.098 --> 00:02:15.401
So, this is so exciting that
you're in the new "Matrix" film.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.036
-So excited.
-Do you have a --

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:19.872
Because I have such
a specific memory of seeing it

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:21.941
in the cinema
for the first time.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.442
Do you remember going to see it?

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.644
-I do. I think I was 16.

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:26.912
I was in the States.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.115
I remember seeing it
with friends.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.382
I think I was in Newton
or something.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.151
I'm not really sure.
That's fuzzy.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:36.356
But what's not fuzzy is
trying to wear only black after

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.892
or not smiling
because I wanted to be cool

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.727
or wearing those sunglasses

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.497
and trying to talk about
existential theories

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.765
when I didn't even understand
what the word meant.

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:50.136
[ Laughter ]
But it really shifted me,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.405
and it shifted my expectations
from cinema.

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:56.075
-Yeah.
-After Neo's bullet trick

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.244
and just the spoon bending
and the mouth stitching,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.912
which was terrifying
and still is.

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:04.416
But it was just like I had
such larger expectations

00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:05.651
when I watched movies.

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:08.454
-Yeah, and I remember,
I was older than you...

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.623
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.991
...I got a little stoned
when I went and saw "Matrix,"

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.794
'cause I heard -- people said,
"You want to get stoned."

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.229
And I maybe got
a little too stoned 'cause it is

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.598
the clearest memory I have
of the only movie I was in

00:03:19.598 --> 00:03:21.133
where at some point
I thought to myself,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.669
"I think this might be real."

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.038
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:26.505
-"I think it might be real."

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:29.475
Also, it was the turn of the
century when the movie came out.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:32.411
Whoever remembers this,
just don't remind me of my age.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:35.147
But, yes, you know the Y2K fear?
-Yeah.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:38.184
-And everyone was like --
Technology was kind of scary,

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.186
it's gonna take over the world,
and there comes "The Matrix"

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.754
and tells you that you might
be living in one,

00:03:42.754 --> 00:03:44.156
so it was terrifying.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.258
-And now you were like,
"Oh, no."

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:47.760
I feel like, five years ago,
we're like,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.194
"No, technology is fine.

00:03:49.194 --> 00:03:51.230
It's all like your aunt
posting stuff on Facebook."

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.898
And then you're like, "Oh, no."
-Yep.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.467
-"I think that's the Matrix."
-Especially when you're having

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.337
a conversation with your friend
and then they log on Instagram

00:03:58.337 --> 00:04:00.339
and the ads pop up,
and you're like,

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:03.976
[ Gasps ] "Did you just
recommend that same toothbrush

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.546
that I was talking about to
my friend five minutes ago?"

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:08.248
-It's crazy.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.815
My wife is constantly
talking about

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:12.318
how she's getting targeted ads.
-I'm fully, fully paranoid.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.119
-Yeah, and then she always
walks to me

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:15.421
and she's like,
"I got another ad.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.757
Have you been talking about
Batman action figures

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.225
around my phone?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.594
And I'm like,
"Uh, uh, duh, uh, kids."

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.095
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:26.666
You talked about
using the Matrix language

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.000
after seeing the first film.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.470
Obviously being in the film,
you have to deliver it.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.940
Was it the same sort of wordy,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.276
thoughtful dialogue
that we've come to expect?

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:41.514
-Yes, and I have lots of words,
and Matrix words.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.149
-Yeah.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.650
-I mean, I don't want Lana
to fire me,

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.086
but now I'm in the movie.
She can't take me out.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:49.021
-Well, no, actually,
with their digital effects,

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.456
they could replace you
like that, yeah.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.590
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.193
-The first day I was filming
was crazy.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.329
I had to say all the lines
that I have in the movie,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.765
which when you guys watch
the movie in the theater

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:02.735
on the 22nd, you will see that
it's wordy,

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.437
but at the same time,
Lana wanted --

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:07.440
Lana Wachowski, the director --
is very --

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.674
She doesn't like rehearsals.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.143
She doesn't like actors
to be prepared.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.078
She likes a really live,
electric environment,

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:16.482
so she wanted me to say all
my lines in the entire movie

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:19.485
in one sunset because she wanted
that perfect, magic light.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:20.519
-Wow.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.855
-And that's 45 minutes
to an hour.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.291
And I had the whole cast
standing in front of me.

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.658
Everyone.

00:05:26.658 --> 00:05:29.261
And my hands were sweaty,
my knees were buckling.

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:31.630
-I mean, every part of that
is terrible,

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:34.833
but especially the fact that
your light is going away.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.235
-I know, I know.
I can see it. I can see it.

00:05:37.235 --> 00:05:39.138
-You can't be like, "I'm gonna
need 15 more minutes.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.406
Somebody get to work
on the sun."

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.008
[ Laughter ]
-No. It's a ticking time bomb.

00:05:43.008 --> 00:05:44.377
And you're like,
"[Bleep] I can see it.

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:45.511
Get it right, get it right."

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:46.945
-I'm sure everything was
a little bit easier

00:05:46.945 --> 00:05:47.947
after you did that first,
though.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.048
-Yeah, after that first day,

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.516
everything was so much easier.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.951
-That's great.
I have more to ask you.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:55.254
We'll be right back with more
from Priyanka Chopra Jonas.

